# CASM WP38 trusted reference: casmorg1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmorg1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake ("LDA #$01", no .ORG). NOT produced
# by CASM. This fixture predates WP38 (Phase 4 WP13) and was originally a
# diagnostic-only fixture expecting CASM_DIAG_ORG_REQUIRED, since .ORG was
# mandatory at the time -- see brain/walkthroughs/2026-07-17-casm-phase4-wp13-directives-emission.md.
# WP38 makes .ORG optional and defaults a no-.ORG assembly to relocatable
# mode at CASM_DEFAULT_ORIGIN ($3400), so casmorg1 now assembles
# successfully and gains a real trusted reference. This is the intended
# effect of WP38, not a regression. Cross-check:
#   - brain/plans/2026-07-24-casm-phase8-wp38-default-origin-and-static-override.md
#
# WP41 -- updated with the R6 footer. "LDA #$01" is a plain numeric
# immediate operand -- no symbol reference at all, so CASM_PARSER_STMT_RELOCATABLE
# is never set and the relocation table is empty (0 entries). The footer
# is still appended (relocatable mode, per CasmRelocatableMode), just with
# a zero-length table. Cross-check:
#   - brain/plans/2026-07-25-casm-phase8-wp41-r6-footer-serialization.md
#
# Source (no .ORG) and hand assembly:
#   00 34        PRG load-address header ($3400, little-endian -- the
#                default relocatable origin, no PC advance)
#   A9 01        LDA #$01
#   [table: 0 entries, nothing emitted]
#   00 34        R6 footer: base address ($3400, little-endian)
#   00 00        R6 footer: relocation entry count (0)
#   52 36        R6 footer: ASCII magic "R6"
#
# bytes: 10
# sha256: 3066f43287eb88722f466e68f92ebcdfd627c790e15d2cb3bb61fff9dd66f79f
